import{_ as a,o as t,c as i,a5 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Test plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/subscription-webhook-corrections/test.md","filePath":"feature/subscription-webhook-corrections/test.md"}'),r={name:"feature/subscription-webhook-corrections/test.md"};function o(s,e,l,c,d,p){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="test-plan" tabindex="-1">Test plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#test-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Test plan&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Seams: actual AgencyBillingService public create/order/webhook methods through Spring transaction proxy and PostgreSQL; existing local QA API endpoints plus SQL financial oracle. These are the previously accepted seams. No collaborator mocks for transactional behavior.</p><ol><li>Same id/same payload: one payment/period/grant/outbox. Same id/amount changed: unchanged original hash/financial state, durable warning/audit.</li><li>Changed duplicate content to unknown code or another agency: original event warning/audit, no new fulfillment or cross-agency link.</li><li>Equivalent numeric scale/timezone timestamp: idempotent without false conflict.</li><li>Audit write failure: exception/rollback, retry after fault removal records evidence once; original payment remains unchanged.</li><li>paidAt before expiry: pending and polled EXPIRED both fulfill once. paidAt at/after expiry, missing/bad date, bad amount remain review.</li><li>Concurrent duplicate callbacks and replay after late fulfillment: one financial effect.</li><li>A conflicting already-purchased plan/future period keeps late order in review with reason.</li><li>Existing QA TX-04/TX-09 expected unchanged; run dependent mutation load only after all prerequisites PASS. Report skip/BLOCKED honestly.</li></ol><p>Actual execution results: see verification below.</p><ol start="9"><li>Distinct event IDs on the same fulfilled order: two stored payments (one VERIFIED, one REVIEW_REQUIRED), one period/grant/outbox and original attempt SUCCEEDED. AB-10 exposed the original attempt being overwritten to UNKNOWN; expected is unchanged.</li></ol><h2 id="actual-results" tabindex="-1">Actual results <a class="header-anchor" href="#actual-results" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Actual results&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Business suite: 1093 registered, 1020 executed PASS, 73 existing gated skips, no failures/errors. All 11 new PostgreSQL Testcontainers regressions PASS. QA webhook-fix-complete: 26 selected cases PASS including AB-06–10 and TX-06; 22 cases not selected. Both primary bugs and additional AB-10 bug demonstrated RED before their production fix.</p><p>Commands: <code>mvn test -Dapi.version=1.44</code> in business-service; QA commands and raw per-case evidence are in <code>qa/payment/README.md</code> and <code>qa/payment/reports/webhook-fix-complete/</code>. Final report: <code>qa/payment/reports/webhook-fix-complete/fix-summary.md</code>.</p><p>Harness correction: TX-04 previously froze event.last_error while requiring a warning. It now freezes financial/order/wallet effects and separately verifies original event hash/status/identity plus durable warning/audit. Expected business behavior did not change. Deadline equality fixture was aligned with PostgreSQL timestamp precision. Narrow test context excludes application auto-configuration.</p><h2 id="standards" tabindex="-1">Standards <a class="header-anchor" href="#standards" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Standards&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Wildcard imports and abbreviated variables corrected; final static review reports no hard safety/transaction blocker.</p><h2 id="spec" tabindex="-1">Spec <a class="header-anchor" href="#spec" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Spec&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Global duplicate detection, canonical/exact legacy replay, audit rollback, cross-agency isolation and late-expiry behavior match the accepted policy. Additional-payment review preserves original successful attempt. Original reports retained, no source business expectations relaxed, no commit/push.</p>',13)])])}const h=a(r,[["render",o]]);export{m as __pageData,h as default};
